{"name":"Black Slug","hex":"#332211","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black slug","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An omnivorous slug found in Europe and the Pacific Northwest, Arion ater, not always black, despite the name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black_slug"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arion ater","blocks":[{"text":"Arion ater, the black slug, is a large terrestrial gastropod mollusk in the family Arionidae, the round back slugs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Arion_ater.jpg/330px-Arion_ater.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arion_ater"},{"title":"Slug","blocks":[{"text":"Slug or land slug is a common name for any apparently shell-less terrestrial gastropod mollusc. The word slug is also often used as part of the common name of any gastropod mollusc that has no shell, a very reduced shell, or only a small internal shell, particularly sea slugs and semi-slugs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Slugs_1896.png/330px-Slugs_1896.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slug"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikiped